  <processInformation>
    <dataSetInformation>
      <common:UUID>c8326692-ca9a-4b37-89ce-3a8a9122f796</common:UUID>
      <name>
        <baseName xml:lang="en">Electricity bioliquids, combustion, at plant</baseName>
      </name>
      <common:synonyms>Elettricità da bioliquidi</common:synonyms>
      <classificationInformation>
        <common:classification name="ILCDCategories" classes="../ILCDClassification.xml">
          <common:class level="0">Energy carriers and technologies</common:class>
          <common:class level="1">Electricity</common:class>
        </common:classification>
      </classificationInformation>
      <common:generalComment>The dataset was developed within the Arcadia Project and was subjected to an internal critical revision. The dataset is related to the production of electricity from biooil derived from seeds, and derived vegetables oil and animal fats, at plants with a nominal power of 500 MW.</common:generalComment>
      <referenceToExternalDocumentation type="source data set" refObjectId="1b89b957-ad3b-4719-8a2b-8f4244bbc66d" version="01.00.000" uri="../sources/1b89b957-ad3b-4719-8a2b-8f4244bbc66d.xml">
        <common:shortDescription>“LA FILIERA DEI BIOLIQUIDI PER LA PRODUZIONE DI ENERGIA ELETTRICA IN ITALIA”&#13;
&#13;
Authors: Tiziana Beltrani, Silvia Sbaffoni, Antonio Picarelli, Gabriella Fiorentino e Amalia Zucaro&#13;
Internal report ARCADIA Project. Background datasets from Ecoinvent database cut-off (v. 3.7.1) were used for the LCA study.&#13;
</common:shortDescription>
      </referenceToExternalDocumentation>
    </dataSetInformation>
    <quantitativeReference type="Reference flow(s)">
      <referenceToReferenceFlow>0</referenceToReferenceFlow>
    </quantitativeReference>
    <time>
      <common:referenceYear>2020</common:referenceYear>
      <common:dataSetValidUntil>2025</common:dataSetValidUntil>
    </time>
    <geography>
      <locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction location="IT">
        <descriptionOfRestrictions>Italy</descriptionOfRestrictions>
      </locationOfOperationSupplyOrProduction>
    </geography>
    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>The dataset is referred to a system including the conversion of biooil to energy (electrical), by means of combustion (500 MW plant).&#13;
.&#13;
The power of the combustion plant is 500 MW named “Oil power plant, 500MW {GLO}| market for | Cut-off, U”.&#13;
The data concerning the sinks of biooil are obtained by secondary data, in accordance with the GSE (Gestore Servizi Energetici) report, "Statistical Report 2020 on Renewable Energy Sources.&#13;
Background data and processes (biooil production and conversion plants) were modelled according to EcoInvent database (v. 3.7.1) cut-off datasets were used. </technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>Electricity from bioliquids sold to Italian electric grid.</technologicalApplicability>
    </technology>
  </processInformation>
